### Scenario 6 - mixed payment (points + card) and declined card (number ending with 0000)
### Customer 1 has 5000 points. 2 x ELC-3002 at GOLD price: goodsHt 160.20, totalTtc 192.24
### 1000 points = 50 EUR (<= 50% of goodsTtc). Paid by card: 142.24. Points earned: floor(160.20 * (1 - 50/192.24)) = 118

@order = http://localhost:8083
@customer = http://localhost:8082

# @name cart
POST {{order}}/carts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 1 }

###
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "ELC-3002", "qty": 2 }

###
# @name checkout
POST {{order}}/carts/{{cart.response.body.id}}/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "shippingMethod": "STANDARD" }

### Declined card: the order stays VALIDATED
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "CARD", "cardNumber": "4111111111110000", "loyaltyPoints": 1000 }

### Not a multiple of 100 -> refused
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "CARD", "cardNumber": "4111111111111111", "loyaltyPoints": 150 }

### More than 50% of the goods -> refused by customer-service
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "CARD", "cardNumber": "4111111111111111", "loyaltyPoints": 5000 }

### Balance is untouched so far
GET {{customer}}/customers/1/loyalty

### Mixed payment succeeds
POST {{order}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.id}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "CARD", "cardNumber": "4111111111111111", "loyaltyPoints": 1000 }

### Balance: 5000 - 1000 + 118
GET {{customer}}/customers/1/loyalty
